From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Asius <dev@asius.ai>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: calibrate Dragon external USB3 TX

The default transmit setting gives USB transaction errors on the external
USB-C path with a long Chestnut cable. Select the 6 dB mode and its QMP v4
tap value of 31, leaving receiver calibration at the SoC defaults.

The tested Dragon passed 8 GiB of byte-verified transfers in each direction
and three independent GPU startups and model replays with this setting.
A subsequent post-boot trial failed a control transfer, so this remains
experimental and does not establish reliable long-cable operation.
Only the external controller and PHY opt into the calibration.

Signed-off-by: Asius <dev@asius.ai>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-radxa-dragon-q6a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-radxa-dragon-q6a.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-radxa-dragon-q6a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-radxa-dragon-q6a.dts
@@ -1326,6 +1326,9 @@
 &usb_1 {
 	status = "okay";
 	dr_mode = "host";
+	/* Use the calibrated 6 dB setting on the external SuperSpeed path. */
+	snps,tx_de_emphasis_quirk;
+	snps,tx_de_emphasis = /bits/ 8 <0>;
 };
 
 &usb_1_dwc3_hs {
@@ -1343,6 +1346,7 @@
 &usb_1_qmpphy {
 	vdda-phy-supply = <&vreg_l6b_1p2>;
 	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l1b_0p912>;
+	qcom,tx-deemph-6db = <31>;
 
 	/delete-property/ orientation-switch;
 
